{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'gh issue view 19 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --comments && gh pr view 22 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --comments && git diff --check 122ce64..HEAD && git diff --stat 122ce64..HEAD && git diff 122ce64..HEAD'","aggregated_output":" README.md                      |  15 ++++-\n scripts/verify_phase1_apply.py |   2 +-\n src/vgt/analysis.py            |  49 +++++++++++++++-\n src/vgt/sidecar.py             |  42 +++++++++++--\n tests/test_analysis.py         | 130 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n tests/test_reascript.py        |   6 +-\n 6 files changed, 227 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex cc69f14..055c63d 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -110,6 +110,16 @@ Every run also renders a **chord-sheet artifact** —\n `<project>.vgt-chords.txt`, next to the sidecar — a plain-text timestamp +\n chord-label listing for by-eye verification.\n \n+The `chords` stage stores two parallel chord lists: `value` (the effective,\n+human-correctable chords used everywhere else — apply, the chord sheet) and\n+`detected` (the pristine machine detection, untouched by corrections). With\n+no corrections the two are equal. Once `value` is human-verified it freezes\n+for good, but `detected` keeps tracking the current reference audio and\n+detector settings on every `vgt analyze` run — it's the machine baseline, so\n+it stays live even while the human's `value` is frozen. Keeping both around\n+is what makes a future \"restore the original detection over this time\n+range\" action possible.\n+\n ### Sections\n \n The `sections` stage detects song-structure boundaries + generic labels\n@@ -181,8 +191,9 @@ for the same pointer from the CLI). It scans the `[vgt] Chords` track's items\n — position, length, take name — by GUID against the sidecar's\n `managed_track_guids`, so it only ever reads objects vgt itself created, and\n writes them back into the sidecar as `analysis.chords.value.segments` with\n-`chords.human_verified: true`. Every other analysis stage (tempo, key,\n-sections) and the rest of the sidecar are left untouched.\n+`chords.human_verified: true`. It never touches `analysis.chords.detected` —\n+the original machine detection stays available there — nor any other\n+analysis stage (tempo, key, sections) or the rest of the sidecar.\n \n From then on: `vgt analyze` skips the chords stage (human-verified stages are\n never recomputed), and re-running the apply ReaScript repaints `[vgt] Chords`\ndiff --git a/scripts/verify_phase1_apply.py b/scripts/verify_phase1_apply.py\nindex 0e8a9ac..f88c016 100644\n--- a/scripts/verify_phase1_apply.py\n+++ b/scripts/verify_phase1_apply.py\n@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@ def verify(project_path: Path, baseline_path: Path, *, first_snapshot: dict[str,\n     except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n         raise VerificationError(f\"cannot read a valid sidecar: {error}\") from error\n     analysis = sidecar.get(\"analysis\")\n-    if sidecar.get(\"schema_version\") != 2 or not isinstance(analysis, dict):\n+    if sidecar.get(\"schema_version\") not in (2, 3) or not isinstance(analysis, dict):\n         _fail(\"Phase 1 sidecar analysis is missing\")\n \n     rpp_text = project_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\ndiff --git a/src/vgt/analysis.py b/src/vgt/analysis.py\nindex d3e6162..860eb0d 100644\n--- a/src/vgt/analysis.py\n+++ b/src/vgt/analysis.py\n@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ from __future__ import annotations\n \n from pathlib import Path\n from typing import Any, Callable\n+import copy\n import hashlib\n import json\n \n@@ -84,6 +85,51 @@ def detect_sections(project_path: Path, source: Path, settings: dict[str, Any],\n     return sections_value\n \n \n+def _refresh_chords_stage(\n+    stage: dict[str, Any],\n+    *,\n+    input_hash: str,\n+    settings_hash: str,\n+    compute: Callable[[], Any],\n+    force: bool = False,\n+) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+    \"\"\"Like `sidecar.refresh_stage`, but tracks `detected` -- the pristine\n+    machine-detection baseline -- independently of `value`.\n+\n+    Before a human verifies `value`, the two are recomputed together (there\n+    is only one detector call; `detected` is just the pristine copy of its\n+    result), same as `refresh_stage`.\n+\n+    Once a human has verified `value`, `refresh_stage` freezes it for good --\n+    but `detected` keeps tracking the current audio/settings via its own\n+    `detected_input_hash`/`detected_settings_hash` pair, recomputing whenever\n+    those change (or `force`). `value` and `human_verified` are never touched\n+    by that recompute; only `detected` moves, preserving the human's\n+    correction while keeping the machine baseline current (#19).\"\"\"\n+    if not stage.get(\"human_verified\"):\n+        refreshed = refresh_stage(stage, input_hash=input_hash, settings_hash=settings_hash, compute=compute, force=force)\n+        if refreshed is stage:\n+            return stage\n+        return {\n+            **refreshed,\n+            \"detected\": copy.deepcopy(refreshed[\"value\"]),\n+            \"detected_input_hash\": input_hash,\n+            \"detected_settings_hash\": settings_hash,\n+        }\n+\n+    detected_is_current = (\n+        stage.get(\"detected_input_hash\") == input_hash and stage.get(\"detected_settings_hash\") == settings_hash\n+    )\n+    if not force and detected_is_current:\n+        return stage\n+    return {\n+        **stage,\n+        \"detected\": compute(),\n+        \"detected_input_hash\": input_hash,\n+        \"detected_settings_hash\": settings_hash,\n+    }\n+\n+\n def _tempo_beat_times(tempo_value: dict[str, Any] | None, source: Path) -> list[float]:\n     \"\"\"Beat timestamps backing the chords stage's grid alignment: reused from\n     the tempo stage's persisted value when present, otherwise (e.g. after a\n@@ -180,7 +226,8 @@ def analyze(\n             emit(f\"[{position}/{total}] {stage} — re-analyzing (forced)…\")\n         else:\n             emit(f\"[{position}/{total}] {stage} — analyzing…\")\n-        analysis[stage] = refresh_stage(\n+        refresh = _refresh_chords_stage if stage == \"chords\" else refresh_stage\n+        analysis[stage] = refresh(\n             analysis[stage],\n             input_hash=input_hash,\n             settings_hash=settings_hash,\ndiff --git a/src/vgt/sidecar.py b/src/vgt/sidecar.py\nindex 7101b2d..f4e22a6 100644\n--- a/src/vgt/sidecar.py\n+++ b/src/vgt/sidecar.py\n@@ -6,6 +6,12 @@ Schema versions:\n   2 -- Phase 1 adds `analysis`: one entry per detector (tempo/key/sections/chords),\n        each cached on an input+settings hash so re-running only recomputes stages\n        whose inputs changed, and a `provenance` block recording the tool/version.\n+  3 -- The `chords` stage gains a `detected` sibling of `value` holding the\n+       pristine machine-detected chords, so a human correction to `value`\n+       never destroys the original detection (#19). Existing v2 sidecars are\n+       migrated by backfilling `detected` from `value` (best effort -- if a\n+       human had already corrected `value` under v2, the true original is\n+       gone and the backfill just seeds `detected` with the corrected chords).\n \n Every stage entry has the same shape:\n   {\n@@ -17,15 +23,28 @@ Every stage entry has the same shape:\n A human correction is applied by setting \"value\" and \"human_verified\": true;\n `refresh_stage` then leaves it untouched on every later re-run regardless of\n whether the input or settings hash changed.\n+\n+The `chords` stage additionally carries:\n+  {\n+    \"detected\": <machine-detected chords, independent of human corrections>,\n+    \"detected_input_hash\": str | null,    # hash `detected` was last computed against\n+    \"detected_settings_hash\": str | null,\n+  }\n+`detected` is never touched by `read-chords`; only `vgt analyze`'s detector\n+writes it. Unlike `value`, `detected` keeps tracking the current audio and\n+settings via its own hash pair even once `value` is human-verified and\n+frozen -- it is the machine baseline, so it stays live, while the human's\n+`value` is what freezes (see `analysis.py`'s `_refresh_chords_stage`).\n \"\"\"\n \n from __future__ import annotations\n \n from pathlib import Path\n from typing import Any, Callable\n+import copy\n import json\n \n-SCHEMA_VERSION = 2\n+SCHEMA_VERSION = 3\n \n ANALYSIS_STAGES = (\"tempo\", \"key\", \"sections\", \"chords\")\n \n@@ -43,8 +62,12 @@ def _empty_stage() -> dict[str, Any]:\n     return {\"value\": None, \"human_verified\": False, \"input_hash\": None, \"settings_hash\": None}\n \n \n+def _empty_chords_stage() -> dict[str, Any]:\n+    return {**_empty_stage(), \"detected\": None, \"detected_input_hash\": None, \"detected_settings_hash\": None}\n+\n+\n def read_sidecar(project_path: str | Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n-    \"\"\"Read the sidecar for `project_path`, upgrading schema v1 to v2 in memory.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Read the sidecar for `project_path`, upgrading older schema versions in memory.\"\"\"\n     path = sidecar_path(project_path)\n     if not path.is_file():\n         raise SidecarError(f\"No .vgt sidecar found at {path}; run the Phase 0 apply action first.\")\n@@ -53,12 +76,23 @@ def read_sidecar(project_path: str | Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n \n \n def upgrade(data: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n-    \"\"\"Return `data` with all Phase 0 fields intact and a v2 `analysis` block present.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Return `data` with all older fields intact and a current-schema `analysis` block present.\"\"\"\n     upgraded = dict(data)\n     upgraded[\"schema_version\"] = SCHEMA_VERSION\n     analysis = dict(upgraded.get(\"analysis\") or {})\n     for stage in ANALYSIS_STAGES:\n-        analysis[stage] = {**_empty_stage(), **(analysis.get(stage) or {})}\n+        if stage == \"chords\":\n+            merged = {**_empty_chords_stage(), **(analysis.get(stage) or {})}\n+            if merged[\"detected\"] is None and merged[\"value\"] is not None:\n+                # v2 -> v3 migration: best-effort backfill, see module docstring.\n+                # Assume `detected` was last computed alongside `value`, so it\n+                # inherits `value`'s hash pair rather than starting stale.\n+                merged[\"detected\"] = copy.deepcopy(merged[\"value\"])\n+                merged[\"detected_input_hash\"] = merged[\"input_hash\"]\n+                merged[\"detected_settings_hash\"] = merged[\"settings_hash\"]\n+            analysis[stage] = merged\n+        else:\n+            analysis[stage] = {**_empty_stage(), **(analysis.get(stage) or {})}\n     analysis.setdefault(\"provenance\", {\"tool\": \"vgt\", \"version\": None, \"settings\": {}})\n     upgraded[\"analysis\"] = analysis\n     return upgraded\ndiff --git a/tests/test_analysis.py b/tests/test_analysis.py\nindex 2a0171a..2665b6d 100644\n--- a/tests/test_analysis.py\n+++ b/tests/test_analysis.py\n@@ -47,19 +47,67 @@ def test_upgrade_keeps_v1_fields_and_adds_v2_analysis_skeleton() -> None:\n         \"config\": {\"reference_track_guid\": REFERENCE_GUID},\n     }\n \n-    v2 = upgrade(v1)\n+    upgraded = upgrade(v1)\n \n-    assert v2[\"schema_version\"] == 2\n-    assert v2[\"managed_track_guids\"] == [\"{AAAA}\", \"{BBBB}\"]\n-    assert v2[\"config\"] == {\"reference_track_guid\": REFERENCE_GUID}\n+    assert upgraded[\"schema_version\"] == 3\n+    assert upgraded[\"managed_track_guids\"] == [\"{AAAA}\", \"{BBBB}\"]\n+    assert upgraded[\"config\"] == {\"reference_track_guid\": REFERENCE_GUID}\n     for stage in ANALYSIS_STAGES:\n-        assert v2[\"analysis\"][stage] == {\n+        expected = {\n             \"value\": None,\n             \"human_verified\": False,\n             \"input_hash\": None,\n             \"settings_hash\": None,\n         }\n-    assert v2[\"analysis\"][\"provenance\"][\"tool\"] == \"vgt\"\n+        if stage == \"chords\":\n+            expected[\"detected\"] = None\n+            expected[\"detected_input_hash\"] = None\n+            expected[\"detected_settings_hash\"] = None\n+        assert upgraded[\"analysis\"][stage] == expected\n+    assert upgraded[\"analysis\"][\"provenance\"][\"tool\"] == \"vgt\"\n+\n+\n+def test_upgrade_backfills_detected_from_value_for_v2_chords() -> None:\n+    \"\"\"A v2 sidecar has no `detected` field on the chords stage -- the v2 -> v3\n+    migration seeds it from `value` (best effort; if `value` was already a\n+    human correction, the true original detection is unrecoverable).\"\"\"\n+    v2 = {\n+        \"schema_version\": 2,\n+        \"config\": {\"reference_track_guid\": REFERENCE_GUID},\n+        \"analysis\": {\n+            \"chords\": {\n+                \"value\": {\"segments\": [{\"start_seconds\": 0.0, \"end_seconds\": 1.0, \"chord\": \"C\"}]},\n+                \"human_verified\": True,\n+                \"input_hash\": \"abc\",\n+                \"settings_hash\": \"def\",\n+            }\n+        },\n+    }\n+\n+    upgraded = upgrade(v2)\n+\n+    chords = upgraded[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"]\n+    assert chords[\"detected\"] == chords[\"value\"]\n+    assert chords[\"detected\"] is not chords[\"value\"]  # backfill copies, doesn't alias\n+\n+\n+def test_upgrade_does_not_clobber_an_existing_detected_field() -> None:\n+    v3 = {\n+        \"schema_version\": 3,\n+        \"analysis\": {\n+            \"chords\": {\n+                \"value\": {\"segments\": [{\"start_seconds\": 0.0, \"end_seconds\": 1.0, \"chord\": \"C\"}]},\n+                \"detected\": {\"segments\": [{\"start_seconds\": 0.0, \"end_seconds\": 1.0, \"chord\": \"G\"}]},\n+                \"human_verified\": True,\n+                \"input_hash\": \"abc\",\n+                \"settings_hash\": \"def\",\n+            }\n+        },\n+    }\n+\n+    upgraded = upgrade(v3)\n+\n+    assert upgraded[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"detected\"][\"segments\"][0][\"chord\"] == \"G\"\n \n \n def test_analyze_requires_an_existing_sidecar(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n@@ -75,7 +123,7 @@ def test_analyze_writes_v2_sidecar_with_skeleton_and_provenance(tmp_path: Path)\n \n     result = analyze(project)\n \n-    assert result[\"schema_version\"] == 2\n+    assert result[\"schema_version\"] == 3\n     assert result[\"managed_track_guids\"] == [\"{AAAA}\", \"{BBBB}\"]  # phase 0 fields intact\n     for stage in ANALYSIS_STAGES:\n         assert result[\"analysis\"][stage][\"input_hash\"] is not None\n@@ -123,6 +171,9 @@ def test_analyze_writes_v2_sidecar_with_skeleton_and_provenance(tmp_path: Path)\n     chord_sheet = project.with_name(chords[\"chord_sheet_path\"])\n     assert chord_sheet.is_file()\n \n+    # No correction has been made yet, so `detected` mirrors `value` exactly.\n+    assert result[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"detected\"] == chords\n+\n     on_disk = read_sidecar(project)\n     assert on_disk == result\n \n@@ -255,6 +306,69 @@ def test_key_and_chord_corrections_survive_rerun(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n     assert result[\"analysis\"][\"key\"][\"human_verified\"] is True\n     assert result[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"value\"] == corrected_chords\n     assert result[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"human_verified\"] is True\n+    # The original detection (backfilled from `value` since this sidecar was\n+    # written without a `detected` field) is preserved, not overwritten by\n+    # the correction.\n+    assert result[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"detected\"] == corrected_chords\n+\n+\n+def test_read_chords_style_correction_preserves_original_detected(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Mirrors what `vgt_read_chords.lua` does: overwrite only\n+    `value.segments` and set `human_verified`, leaving `detected` (and every\n+    other field the detector wrote) untouched -- the core guarantee #19\n+    adds. A subsequent `analyze()` with unchanged audio/settings must not\n+    recompute `detected` either -- it only tracks the current inputs, and\n+    they haven't moved (see the sibling test below for the case where they\n+    do).\"\"\"\n+    project = _project_copy(tmp_path)\n+    _write_v1_sidecar(project)\n+    first = analyze(project)\n+\n+    original_detected = first[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"detected\"]\n+    assert original_detected == first[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"value\"]\n+\n+    sidecar = read_sidecar(project)\n+    corrected_segments = [{\"start_seconds\": 0.0, \"end_seconds\": 1.0, \"chord\": \"C:maj\"}]\n+    sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"value\"][\"segments\"] = corrected_segments\n+    sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"human_verified\"] = True\n+    write_sidecar(project, sidecar)\n+\n+    result = analyze(project)\n+\n+    chords = result[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"]\n+    assert chords[\"value\"][\"segments\"] == corrected_segments\n+    assert chords[\"human_verified\"] is True\n+    assert chords[\"detected\"] == original_detected\n+    assert chords[\"detected\"][\"segments\"] != corrected_segments\n+\n+\n+def test_detected_keeps_refreshing_against_current_settings_once_value_is_human_verified(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Per #19's design leaning: `detected` is the machine baseline and stays\n+    live -- even once `value` is human-verified and frozen, a settings change\n+    still recomputes `detected` (while `value`/`human_verified` don't move).\n+    The detector is deterministic given the same audio, so the recomputed\n+    `detected.segments` come out identical -- what's observable is that the\n+    recompute actually ran, tracked by `detected_settings_hash` moving to the\n+    new settings hash instead of staying pinned to the stale one.\"\"\"\n+    project = _project_copy(tmp_path)\n+    _write_v1_sidecar(project)\n+    analyze(project)\n+\n+    sidecar = read_sidecar(project)\n+    stale_detected_settings_hash = sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"detected_settings_hash\"]\n+    corrected_segments = [{\"start_seconds\": 0.0, \"end_seconds\": 1.0, \"chord\": \"C:maj\"}]\n+    sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"value\"][\"segments\"] = corrected_segments\n+    sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"human_verified\"] = True\n+    write_sidecar(project, sidecar)\n+\n+    # Same audio, but different chord-detector settings -- `detected` should\n+    # track this even though `value` is frozen by the human correction.\n+    result = analyze(project, settings={\"chords\": {\"note\": \"force-recompute\"}})\n+\n+    chords = result[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"]\n+    assert chords[\"value\"][\"segments\"] == corrected_segments\n+    assert chords[\"human_verified\"] is True\n+    assert chords[\"detected_settings_hash\"] != stale_detected_settings_hash\n \n \n def test_section_rename_and_boundary_nudge_survive_rerun(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n@@ -292,4 +406,4 @@ def test_cli_analyze_invocation(tmp_path: Path, capsys: pytest.CaptureFixture[st\n     assert main([\"analyze\", str(project)]) == 0\n \n     output = json.loads(capsys.readouterr().out)\n-    assert output[\"schema_version\"] == 2\n+    assert output[\"schema_version\"] == 3\ndiff --git a/tests/test_reascript.py b/tests/test_reascript.py\nindex 1320690..9db4ce7 100644\n--- a/tests/test_reascript.py\n+++ b/tests/test_reascript.py\n@@ -156,6 +156,7 @@ def test_read_chords_writes_corrected_segments_as_human_verified(tmp_path: Path)\n         \"tempo\": {\"value\": {\"bpm\": 120.0}, \"human_verified\": True, \"input_hash\": \"h1\", \"settings_hash\": \"h2\"},\n         \"chords\": {\n             \"value\": {\"segments\": [{\"start_seconds\": 0.0, \"end_seconds\": 1.0, \"chord\": \"Am\"}], \"vocabulary\": \"maj_min\", \"backend\": \"librosa\"},\n+            \"detected\": {\"segments\": [{\"start_seconds\": 0.0, \"end_seconds\": 1.0, \"chord\": \"Am\"}], \"vocabulary\": \"maj_min\", \"backend\": \"librosa\"},\n             \"human_verified\": False,\n             \"input_hash\": \"old-hash\",\n             \"settings_hash\": \"old-settings\",\n@@ -164,7 +165,7 @@ def test_read_chords_writes_corrected_segments_as_human_verified(tmp_path: Path)\n     sidecar.write_text(\n         json.dumps(\n             {\n-                \"schema_version\": 2,\n+                \"schema_version\": 3,\n                 \"managed_track_guids\": [chords_guid, other_guid],\n                 \"config\": {\"reference_track_guid\": reference_guid},\n                 \"analysis\": analysis,\n@@ -216,10 +217,13 @@ _G.__messages = messages\n             \"vocabulary\": \"maj_min\",\n             \"backend\": \"librosa\",\n         },\n+        \"detected\": analysis[\"chords\"][\"detected\"],\n         \"human_verified\": True,\n         \"input_hash\": \"old-hash\",\n         \"settings_hash\": \"old-settings\",\n     }\n+    # `detected` (the original machine detection) is untouched by the correction.\n+    assert data[\"analysis\"][\"chords\"][\"detected\"] == analysis[\"chords\"][\"detected\"]\n     # The tempo stage (untouched) round-trips byte-for-byte in structure.\n     assert data[\"analysis\"][\"tempo\"] == analysis[\"tempo\"]\n \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"gh pr view 22 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,state,isDraft,baseRefName,headRefName,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,commits,files,body,comments && git diff --check origin/main...HEAD && git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD && rg -n -C 4 'read.chords|detected|schema_version|refresh_stage|chords' src tests README.md docs scripts | head -500 && sed -n '1,340p' src/vgt/analysis.py && sed -n '1,220p' src/vgt/sidecar.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"gh pr view 22 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,state,isDraft,baseRefName,headRefName,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,commits,files,body,comments && git diff --check origin/main...HEAD && git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD && rg -n -C 4 'read.chords|detected|schema_version|refresh_stage|chords' src tests README.md docs scripts | head -500 && sed -n '1,340p' src/vgt/analysis.py && sed -n '1,220p' src/vgt/sidecar.py\"","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"body\":\"Closes #19\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nSee issue #19 for details.\",\"comments\":[],\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-07-19T06:40:05Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"marekkucharski@mini.local\",\"id\":\"\",\"login\":\"\",\"name\":\"Marek Kucharski\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Sonnet 5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-07-19T06:40:05Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…rections\\n\\nAdd a `detected` sibling to `analysis.chords.value` in the .vgt sidecar\\n(schema v2 -> v3) so a human correction to `value` no longer destroys the\\ndetector's original output. `vgt analyze` keeps `detected` in lockstep with\\n`value` on every recompute, and both freeze together once `value` is\\nhuman-verified. `vgt_read_chords.lua` already only ever touched\\n`value.segments` + `human_verified`, so it now leaves `detected` untouched\\nby construction. Existing v2 sidecars are migrated by backfilling `detected`\\nfrom `value` (best effort).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(chords): preserve originally-detected chords alongside human cor…\",\"oid\":\"a876a14852d2644e3c00d663e4d407f974cea473\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-07-19T06:55:19Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"marekkucharski@mini.local\",\"id\":\"\",\"login\":\"\",\"name\":\"Marek Kucharski\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Sonnet 5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-07-19T06:55:19Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…ue is human-verified\\n\\nPer #19's stated design leaning, `detected` is the machine baseline and\\nshould stay live even after a human verifies `value` -- only `value` itself\\nshould freeze. The prior implementation froze `detected` alongside `value`\\non human verification, defeating that intent. `detected` now tracks its own\\n`detected_input_hash`/`detected_settings_hash` pair so `vgt analyze` keeps\\nrecomputing it against the current audio/settings regardless of `value`'s\\nhuman-verified state, while `value`/`human_verified` remain untouched.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(chords): keep detected refreshing against current inputs once val…\",\"oid\":\"6b7e9a7bfd7478721438255252b613985062e7a5\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"additions\":13,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"scripts/verify_phase1_apply.py\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/analysis.py\",\"additions\":48,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/sidecar.py\",\"additions\":38,\"deletions\":4,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"tests/test_analysis.py\",\"additions\":122,\"deletions\":8,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"tests/test_reascript.py\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"headRefName\":\"issue-19-preserve-originally-detected-chords-alon\",\"isDraft\":false,\"mergeStateStatus\":\"CLEAN\",\"number\":22,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Preserve originally-detected chords alongside human corrections (both always available)\"}\n README.md                      |  15 ++++-\n scripts/verify_phase1_apply.py |   2 +-\n src/vgt/analysis.py            |  49 +++++++++++++++-\n src/vgt/sidecar.py             |  42 +++++++++++--\n tests/test_analysis.py         | 130 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n tests/test_reascript.py        |   6 +-\n 6 files changed, 227 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)\ntests/test_project.py-43-    assert main([\"apply\", str(FIXTURE)]) == 2\ntests/test_project.py-44-    assert \"reascript/vgt_initialize.lua\" in capsys.readouterr().err\ntests/test_project.py-45-\ntests/test_project.py-46-\ntests/test_project.py:47:def test_read_chords_command_points_to_the_read_chords_reascript(capsys: pytest.CaptureFixture[str]) -> None:\ntests/test_project.py:48:    assert main([\"read-chords\", str(FIXTURE)]) == 2\ntests/test_project.py-49-    err = capsys.readouterr().err\ntests/test_project.py:50:    assert \"reascript/vgt_read_chords.lua\" in err\ntests/test_project.py-51-    assert \"human-verified\" in err\n--\nREADME.md-38-## Analyze the reference track (Phase 1)\nREADME.md-39-\nREADME.md-40-`vgt analyze [project.rpp]` requires a `.vgt` sidecar already written by the\nREADME.md-41-apply action above. It resolves the reference track's source audio file,\nREADME.md:42:runs the tempo/key/sections/chords detectors, and writes the results back\nREADME.md-43-into the sidecar as schema version 2 — never inside REAPER itself.\nREADME.md-44-\nREADME.md-45-Each detector's output is cached against a hash of the source audio and the\nREADME.md-46-detector's settings, so re-running only recomputes stages whose inputs\n--\nREADME.md-66-  behind this extra precisely so a default install never needs it.\nREADME.md-67-- **Fallback: librosa's `beat_track`** (installed by default) when madmom\nREADME.md-68-  isn't installed, or fails to import. It gives beat times but no\nREADME.md-69-  downbeats, so time signature falls back to a `time_signature_hint`\nREADME.md:70:  setting (or `4/4`) rather than a detected bar length.\nREADME.md-71-\nREADME.md-72-Every run also renders a **click-only artifact** — `<project>.vgt-tempo-click.wav`,\nREADME.md:73:next to the sidecar — a bare click on the detected beat grid (the reference\nREADME.md-74-audio is not mixed in) so the grid can be checked by ear or lined up against\nREADME.md-75-the reference in REAPER; it is vgt-owned and regenerated each run, not\nREADME.md-76-committed alongside the project.\nREADME.md:77:The tempo stage's `value` also stores the raw detected `beat_times` — the\nREADME.md:78:shared beat-synchronous grid the `chords` stage below aligns to.\nREADME.md-79-\nREADME.md:80:### Key & beat-aligned chords\nREADME.md-81-\nREADME.md-82-The `key` stage detects root + scale (major/minor) from the reference\nREADME.md-83-track's full mix:\nREADME.md-84-\n--\nREADME.md-87-  Silicon, so it's never a hard dependency and has no `uv` extra of its own).\nREADME.md-88-- **Fallback: librosa chroma** correlated against the 24 Krumhansl–Schmuckler\nREADME.md-89-  major/minor key templates — always available.\nREADME.md-90-\nREADME.md:91:The `chords` stage detects a beat-aligned maj/min chord sequence, with every\nREADME.md-92-segment boundary snapped onto the `tempo` stage's shared `beat_times` grid\nREADME.md:93:(not a separately detected grid):\nREADME.md-94-\nREADME.md-95-- **Primary backend: madmom**'s CNN chord recognizer, via the same `madmom`\nREADME.md-96-  extra as the tempo stage.\nREADME.md-97-- **Fallback: Chordino**, via the `sonic-annotator` vamp-plugin host, when\n--\nREADME.md-106-collapse to their nearest maj/min match — so every result is flagged\nREADME.md-107-`\"vocabulary\": \"maj_min\"`.\nREADME.md-108-\nREADME.md-109-Every run also renders a **chord-sheet artifact** —\nREADME.md:110:`<project>.vgt-chords.txt`, next to the sidecar — a plain-text timestamp +\nREADME.md-111-chord-label listing for by-eye verification.\nREADME.md-112-\nREADME.md:113:The `chords` stage stores two parallel chord lists: `value` (the effective,\nREADME.md:114:human-correctable chords used everywhere else — apply, the chord sheet) and\nREADME.md:115:`detected` (the pristine machine detection, untouched by corrections). With\nREADME.md-116-no corrections the two are equal. Once `value` is human-verified it freezes\nREADME.md:117:for good, but `detected` keeps tracking the current reference audio and\nREADME.md-118-detector settings on every `vgt analyze` run — it's the machine baseline, so\nREADME.md-119-it stays live even while the human's `value` is frozen. Keeping both around\nREADME.md-120-is what makes a future \"restore the original detection over this time\nREADME.md-121-range\" action possible.\n--\nREADME.md-142-Labels are intentionally generic — renaming them (`\"A\"` → `\"chorus\"`) is a\nREADME.md-143-normal correction, not a failure, and (like every other stage) persists once\nREADME.md-144-`human_verified: true` is set. Every run also renders a **section-timeline\nREADME.md-145-artifact** — `<project>.vgt-sections.txt`, next to the sidecar — so the\nREADME.md:146:detected structure can be checked by eye; it is vgt-owned and regenerated\nREADME.md-147-each run, not committed alongside the project.\nREADME.md-148-\nREADME.md-149-## Apply analysis (Phase 1)\nREADME.md-150-\nREADME.md-151-Run the same ReaScript again after `vgt analyze`. It reads the sidecar and adds\nREADME.md-152-`[vgt]` section regions plus a muted `[vgt] Chords` track whose text items\nREADME.md:153:carry the detected beat-aligned labels. Unlike every other vgt-owned label\nREADME.md-154-track, chord items are left **unlocked** — they are the editing surface for\nREADME.md-155-chord corrections (see below). It sets vgt-owned audio items to time-based\nREADME.md-156-positioning before any tempo changes.\nREADME.md-157-\nREADME.md-158-When REAPER still has exactly its single default 120 BPM / 4/4 tempo marker,\nREADME.md:159:the action writes the detected tempo map. If the project already has any other\nREADME.md-160-tempo map, it leaves that map untouched and instead creates a muted, locked\nREADME.md-161-`[vgt] Beats` item track. Both the regions and vgt tracks are reconciled on\nREADME.md-162-re-apply; no non-`[vgt]` track, region, or item is changed.\nREADME.md-163-\n--\nREADME.md-171-To run the full disposable REAPER proof (including both the default-map and\nREADME.md-172-existing-map branches, each applied twice), use `--run-live` with the same\nREADME.md-173-baseline argument instead of supplying a project path.\nREADME.md-174-\nREADME.md:175:## Correcting chords in REAPER\nREADME.md-176-\nREADME.md:177:Auto-detected chords are sometimes wrong, and correcting raw second-offsets\nREADME.md:178:by hand in the sidecar is awkward. Instead, edit the chords directly on the\nREADME.md-179-`[vgt] Chords` track's timeline — its items are unlocked (though still muted,\nREADME.md-180-so they never play):\nREADME.md-181-\nREADME.md-182-- **rename** an item's take to relabel a chord (e.g. `Am` → `A`);\n--\nREADME.md-184-- **split** an item (REAPER's native split action) to break one chord into two;\nREADME.md-185-- **delete** an item to drop a spurious chord, or **add** a new item (with a\nREADME.md-186-  take name) to insert one.\nREADME.md-187-\nREADME.md:188:When done, load [reascript/vgt_read_chords.lua](reascript/vgt_read_chords.lua)\nREADME.md:189:in REAPER's Action List and run it (or run `vgt read-chords [project.rpp]`\nREADME.md-190-for the same pointer from the CLI). It scans the `[vgt] Chords` track's items\nREADME.md-191-— position, length, take name — by GUID against the sidecar's\nREADME.md-192-`managed_track_guids`, so it only ever reads objects vgt itself created, and\nREADME.md:193:writes them back into the sidecar as `analysis.chords.value.segments` with\nREADME.md:194:`chords.human_verified: true`. It never touches `analysis.chords.detected` —\nREADME.md-195-the original machine detection stays available there — nor any other\nREADME.md-196-analysis stage (tempo, key, sections) or the rest of the sidecar.\nREADME.md-197-\nREADME.md:198:From then on: `vgt analyze` skips the chords stage (human-verified stages are\nREADME.md-199-never recomputed), and re-running the apply ReaScript repaints `[vgt] Chords`\nREADME.md-200-identically from the corrected sidecar — the round trip is idempotent.\n--\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-7-ever recognized -- 7ths, sus, add9, etc. all collapse to their nearest maj/min\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-8-match -- so every result is flagged `\"vocabulary\": \"maj_min\"`.\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-9-\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-10-Beat-alignment: chord segment boundaries are always snapped to the shared\nsrc/vgt/chords.py:11:beat grid detected by the tempo stage (tempo.py, #8) -- `detect_chords` takes\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-12-that grid's beat times as an explicit argument rather than detecting its own,\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-13-so key/chord/tempo all agree on one grid (see `analysis.py`'s\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-14-`_tempo_beat_times`). This applies uniformly to every backend, including\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-15-madmom, whose own chord segmentation isn't beat-quantized.\n--\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-28-class ChordDetectionError(RuntimeError):\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-29-    \"\"\"No backend could produce a chord sequence for the source audio.\"\"\"\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-30-\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-31-\nsrc/vgt/chords.py:32:def _madmom_chords(source: Path) -> list[tuple[float, float, str]] | None:\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-33-    \"\"\"Beat-independent (start, end, label) triples via madmom's CNN chord\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-34-    recognizer, or None if madmom isn't importable, or fails at runtime, in\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-35-    this environment (mirrors tempo.py's madmom fallback rule: import errors\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-36-    and runtime failures both mean \"unusable here\").\"\"\"\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-37-    try:\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-38-        from madmom.audio.chroma import DeepChromaProcessor  # type: ignore[import-not-found]\nsrc/vgt/chords.py:39:        from madmom.features.chords import DeepChromaChordRecognitionProcessor  # type: ignore[import-not-found]\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-40-    except ImportError:\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-41-        return None\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-42-\nsrc/vgt/chords.py-43-    try:\